; Option for opponents to ask for surrender if you're hurt enough
; Based on the stats that are already there? I guess someone who prefers non lethal will be more likely to do that
; Variable thresholds for "hurt enough" depending on the current stats
; More paranoia could maybe make that happen less
; It replaces their attack but if you do attack them instead of surrendering they just knock you/kill you instead
@TGC_NPCDemandSurrender(Surrenderer,Surrendee)
#DIM Surrenderer
#DIM Surrendee

IF Surrendee == MASTER
    PRINTFORML %CALLNAME:Surrenderer% points %HIS_HER(Surrenderer)% %PrintWeaponName(Surrenderer)% at you and demands you to surrender.
    {
        CALL ASK_M(
            "Comply", 1,
            "Resist", 1,
            "TSP and Execute", 1,
            "TSP and Restrain", 1
        )
    }
    SELECTCASE RESULT
    CASE 0
        PRINTFORMW You comply to %CALLNAME:Surrenderer%'s order and place your hands up.
        PRINTFORMW %HE_SHE(Surrenderer,1)% walks over to you and restrains your arms.
    CASE 1
        PRINTFORMW You ignore %CALLNAME:Surrenderer%'s order and continue attacking.
        PRINTFORMW %CALLNAME:Surrenderer% will now attack to \@ nNecro ? kill # knock you out\@ now.
    CASE 2
        PRINTFORMW Using your time powers, you move to %CALLNAME:Surrenderer% and execute %HIM_HER(Surrenderer)%
    CASE 3
        PRINTFORMW Using your time powers, you move to %CALLNAME:Surrenderer% and restrain %HIM_HER(Surrenderer)% using a piece of rope.
        TCVAR:Surrenderer:Grievous_Harm = 1
        SIF !TFLAG:妄想中 && Surrendee != MASTER
        CALL FightLosePenalty((Surrendee),Surrenderer)
        DT_CELL_SET "lcCombatants", GetCombatant(Surrenderer), "nonCombatant", 2, 1
    ENDSELECT
ENDIF

; im thinking of conscious imobolizations as well
; like you shoot off their arm or leg and they will most likely surrender
; and if they can't move then they'll also surrender automaticly
; at max bravery they will not surrender unless they are killed or knocked out
; at no bravery they will surrender if they get hit at all (above a minimum threshold of like 50)
@TGC_WILL_SURRENDER(ARG)

